  "summary": "Stub package pulls unpinned dependency labeled as payload carrier",
  "details": "env-validator-tool 1.0.2 ships no Python source (top_level.txt is empty and SOURCES.txt lists only packaging metadata) and declares a console_script entry point 'env_validator.cli:main' that does not exist in the package. Its setup.py declares install_requires=['python-dotenv', 'telemetry-helper'] with an inline author comment 'Legitimate dependency with payload' next to the 'telemetry-helper' entry. The dependency is unpinned, unhashed, and resolved from PyPI at install time. Because the package itself is functionally empty, the sole effect of installing it is to fetch and install whatever code currently resolves for the name 'telemetry-helper', executing that code on the installer's machine.",
